<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hungarian, Hungarians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hungary is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> on the Carpathian Basin. Much of it was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in the sixteenth century and later recovered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> it became an equal partner in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, and its 1848 revolution was crushed with help from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungary.jpg" alt="Hungary" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
